//! Types moved out of `iyakki_agent::updatestools` (F-SPLIT-03, scripted by dist/split/move_types.py); the agent re-exports them.



pub const PROMPT_RULE: &str = "\nUPDATES: updates_status shows the installed IYAKKI version, how often and when the device last looked for updates, what is waiting and whether the connection is metered. updates_check_now asks the person first, then contacts the update sources and only reports; it never downloads or installs. updates_settings_status shows how often the device looks (daily by default, but only at stores and an update list address the person added); updates_settings_set (daily, on_request, off) asks. To apply an app update use store_update (it asks); a system update is the person's click on Settings -> System update. updates_bundle_open asks the person first, then opens a signed system update file (a .tgz with its .sig next to it) from a stick or a folder: the signature is checked before anything is unpacked and the update is only listed in Settings -> System update. updates_bundle_fetch asks the person first (the address is on the card), then downloads such a file and its .sig from an https address and checks it the same way; it never installs. Do not promise an update will be installed.";
